Q: &quot;Class template has already been defined&quot; when making similar but different specializations A: <p>Clang also rejects this code, but not GCC. This is not the first time I'm seeing problems with <code>std::void_t</code>.</p>
<p>I would stay away from it, and prefer <code>decltype(void(T::A))</code>.</p>
<p>Or you can define your own robust <code>void_t</code> (code taken from <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/void_t" rel="nofollow noreferrer">cppreference</a>):</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;typename... Ts&gt; struct make_void { using type = void; };
template&lt;typename... Ts&gt; using void_t = typename make_void&lt;Ts...&gt;::type;
</code></pre>
